<title>UK: Texaco Netherlands cuts runs at Nerefco refinery.</title>
<headline>Texaco Netherlands cuts runs at Nerefco refinery.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Netherlands said on Tuesday it was cutting runs at the 400,000 barrel per day (bpd) Nerefco refinery it shares with British Petroleum because of poor profit margins.</p>
<p>Texaco, which controls 35 percent of Pernis and the Europoort complex, said it was cutting 10 percent of it crude runs, equivalent to a 14,000 bpd cut.</p>
<p>&quot;Texaco has taken the decision to cut crude runs by 10 percent due to bad margins,&quot; said a company spokesman.</p>
<p>Industry sources said British Petroleum was monitoring the situation closely with regards to its 65 percent share of the plant</p>
